  data: {
    LLM: "Draw trumps early if you have the Ace or Seven. If partner leads a suit and you have the Ace, play it immediately to secure the points unless the trick is already won. Don't be afraid to trump low if you can win.\n\nThe 'Seven' Trap: The King (4 pts) is often sacrificed to save the Seven (10 pts). Don't lead a Seven if the Ace is out.\n\nCounting the 120: If opponents have 60, you can't win. If you have 61, stop risking high cards. Play safe.",
